within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EG02_Everolimus;
model Everolimus "Everolimus — default model: Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference"
  extends Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of everolimus: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.L_AntineoplasticAndImmunomodulatingAgents.L01E_ProteinKinaseInhibitors.L01EG02_Everolimus.Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference\">Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of everolimus in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Everolimus_Hirabatake2022_reference</code></li><li><code>Everolimus_Moes2012_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About everolimus</h4><p>Everolimus is an mTOR inhibitor used as an antineoplastic and immunosuppressant for cancers such as renal cell carcinoma, breast cancer, and neuroendocrine tumors, as well as tuberous sclerosis. It is authorised in the European Union for several cancer types and tuberous sclerosis, and is an approved drug.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421052\">Wikidata Q421052</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Everolimus\">Everolimus</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Everolimus;
